# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# Out-of-tree build dir used when compiling with the Trust toolchain (trustc)
target-trust

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/
.claude/

# Release-cut output (`cargo ship cut` / `--dry-run`): dist/aterm.app, the DMG +
# dSYM + build.txt artifacts, and the resumable cut journal dist/cut-state.toml.
# All regenerable/local — the committed release record is RELEASES.ledger + the
# published GitHub Release, never dist/.
/dist/

# Historical Trust-toolchain .app build output (predates the cutter's in-process
# Trust-rustc lane; kept ignored so stale local dirs never get committed)
/dist-trustc/

# Ad-hoc local DEV bundles (a session's `dist-dev/aterm.app` for A/B runs):
# regenerable build output like dist/, never committed — and, untracked, it
# would otherwise block `pub stage`, which requires the whole tree clean.
/dist-dev/

# Trust verifier per-obligation JSON dump (trustc/tcargo emits one file per fn)
/1/

# Local proof cache written by the Trust verification gate (regenerable)
/.trust-cache/

# Vendored dependency SOURCE must never be swallowed by the build-artifact `debug`
# rule near the top. MEASURED on the winnow fork (retired 2026-08-27 with
# `toml_edit`): it shipped a real `combinator/debug` tracing module, and dropping
# it broke `cargo build` on a fresh checkout. The re-include stays for the NEXT
# vendored crate with a `debug` source directory — the bare `debug` rule still
# covers `target/**/debug`.
!vendor/**/debug/
/target-tippy/

# One-shot Trust/verification campaign scratch — raw sweep logs and gap dumps are
# regenerable evidence, not source. Keep them out of the tree so they stop drifting
# stale against main (removed in the cruft cleanup; see PROOF_CARRYING_PERFORMANCE.md
# for the durable write-up).
sweep*-logs/
/fleet-gaps.json

# rustc / trustc internal-compiler-error crash dumps (auto-named rustc-ice-*.txt / trustc-ice-*.txt)
rustc-ice-*.txt
trustc-ice-*.txt
*.orig
# ... but a VENDORED fork's `Cargo.toml.orig` is upstream PROVENANCE, not a merge
# leftover: it is the manifest as published, and without it the local manifest edits
# cannot be separated from upstream's. The bare rule above made `git add` on those
# paths a silent no-op — the five already tracked pre-date it. Same reasoning as
# `!vendor/**/debug/` above.
!vendor/**/*.orig

# Local publication-engine output (regenerated by ~/publication/bin/pub).
/publish/.out/

# RELEASE SIGNING IS A DEV-ENVIRONMENT CREDENTIAL — never repo content.
# The epoch-2 update-signing key + its config live on the release machine
# only (~/.aterm/, Keychain recovery item; see docs/RELEASING.md "Signing
# authority"). These patterns are a last-ditch stop against an accidental
# in-repo copy ever being staged; tools/grep_guard.sh B6 backstops tracked
# content the same way.
update-v2.key
release.conf
*.ed25519
*.ed25519.priv

# Python bytecode from the art rigs (art/**/*.py are authoring tools, not
# shipped code — their caches are pure build residue).
__pycache__/
*.pyc
